# shared/code/MANIFEST -- every code listing on a slide, and where it came from.
#
# Format:  <output>.txt <TAB> <path relative to prover/> <TAB> <first>-<last>
#
# `make code' (or shared/code/extract.sh) regenerates every .txt from the tree.
# A listing on a slide is therefore the source AS IT STANDS, not a transcription
# of it; when a source file moves under the listing, the regenerated .txt either
# shows the change or the extraction fails loudly.  Line ranges are the fragile
# part -- re-run `make code' and read the diff before every talk.
#
# Verified against the tree on 2026-08-10.  NOTE reference/PROOF-DEBT.md is
# REGENERATED by every library load, so the bills.txt range moves whenever a
# theorem is added or a bill changes -- it is the one entry here that will go
# stale silently, since a wrong-but-valid range extracts the wrong entry rather
# than failing.  Re-read the extracted bills.txt, not just the exit status.

